-- title:
--   The executable regional circuit has exactly the singleton window language
-- statement:
--   For every metric scene slot, the circuit returned by `SingleCodes.regionalCircuit` has a valid root and its ordered language consists exactly of duplicate-free lists whose underlying finite sets are generated by the singleton separator grammar; conversely every generated partition occurs. This is the local semantic induction for the executable bottom-up state table, with all default and empty-component cases included.
-- source:
--   Ravichandran and Reyzin, Exact Sum-of-Radii Clustering under Any Constant Stability, Appendix A.6, pp. 21–22, https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.03547. Soundness and completeness of the singleton dynamic-programming recurrence as implemented by `SingleCircuit.compileRegion`.

